From: zhoufl <zhoufl@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: enable the PPE DRAM FOE table

airoha_ppe_hw_init() programs REG_PPE_TB_HASH_CFG with the DRAM hash
modes but leaves PPE_DRAM_TABLE_EN cleared, so the PPE only searches
the 8192-entry SRAM table while the 16384-entry DRAM table allocated
next to it is never used. With only 8192 effective slots, workloads
with more than 8k concurrent connections (PCDN, bittorrent) saturate
the table and keep churning the software path.

Set PPE_DRAM_TABLE_EN so the full 24576-entry table is searched, and
zero the DRAM region during the initial flush so stale data can never
be interpreted as a valid binding.

Signed-off-by: zhoufl <zhoufl@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -182,6 +182,7 @@
 			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_SRAM_TABLE_EN_MASK, 1) |
 			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_SRAM_HASH1_EN_MASK, 1) |
 			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_SRAM_HASH1_MODE_MASK, 1) |
+			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_DRAM_TABLE_EN_MASK, 1) |
 			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_DRAM_HASH1_MODE_MASK, 3));
 
 		airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_PPE_TB_CFG(i),
@@ -1613,6 +1614,12 @@
 			return err;
 	}
 
+	/* The PPE also searches the DRAM FOE table: make sure stale data
+	 * can never be interpreted as a valid binding.
+	 */
+	memset(hwe + sram_num_entries, 0,
+	       PPE_DRAM_NUM_ENTRIES * sizeof(*hwe));
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
